{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/407153-the-most-wtf-or-why-would-you-do-that-moment-in-your-games","id":407153,"title":"the most WTF or Why would you do that moment in your games?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-15T17:28:42-08:00","id":407153,"title":"the most WTF or Why would you do that moment in your games?","content":"so, any moments that shocked you or your players? they can be funny, hilarious or downright disturbing.<br /> <br /> as for me, im runing a mage game in which a female Hermetic got married with a Female Pooka (changeling, dont ask. fuck the rules xD)..so , they love each other a lot even if they know that The Winter/Ascension is coming..<br /> <br /> So..they love each other, a lot..they are on a Chantry...they love ach other, and they decided to have childrens..and no, adoption is out of the question. Lets just say that my Player knows what is Futanari and he has enough Life points to &quot;Make it Work.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T21:45:19-08:00","id":407383,"title":"","content":"The story was set in 90's an the Vampire pack I was in had just found out that members of the Camarilla have been taking recently turned vampires, put them in bins and sell them to the highest bidder for their blood. Learning that we would've been victims too if some mysterious group hadn't broken us out, we decided to see if the Sabbat had any connection to this. Since we were now considering joining the Sabbat, we were told to &quot;bring back the head of one who is threatening you.&quot; Our Tremere leader decided that his entire chantey's annihilation would be the best proof of loyalty. His idea was to get one of Ennonia's (my character) junkie pilot friends to fly his plane that would be filled with explosives and ram it into the chantry in the morning. The problem was that though the Nosferatu was a leg-breaker, he was still a half-way decent guy and didn't want to do it. Ennonia was just &quot;too chaotic&quot; as a follower who was starting to like the Nosferatu. So we parted ways. So I'd say that' an almost moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T06:50:50-08:00","id":407702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/407153-the-most-wtf-or-why-would-you-do-that-moment-in-your-games?p=407383#post407383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The story was set in 90's an the Vampire pack I was in had just found out that members of the Camarilla have been taking recently turned vampires, put them in bins and sell them to the highest bidder for their blood. Learning that we would've been victims too if some mysterious group hadn't broken us out, we decided to see if the Sabbat had any connection to this. Since we were now considering joining the Sabbat, we were told to &quot;bring back the head of one who is threatening you.&quot; Our Tremere leader decided that his entire chantey's annihilation would be the best proof of loyalty. His idea was to get one of Ennonia's (my character) junkie pilot friends to fly his plane that would be filled with explosives and ram it into the chantry in the morning. The problem was that though the Nosferatu was a leg-breaker, he was still a half-way decent guy and didn't want to do it. Ennonia was just &quot;too chaotic&quot; as a follower who was starting to like the Nosferatu. So we parted ways. So I'd say that' an almost moment.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So he wanted to go Joesph Joestar on his chantery eh XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2256-goblin404","name":"Goblin404","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2256_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T22:29:31-08:00","id":408621,"title":"","content":"While this was in a Renquiem game, the catore were traveling through the sewers until we came across this loser blood cult and we needed to get by them without causing too much trouble. So my Ventrue took off all her clothes, showered with the blood dripping from their latest offering, arose and claimed to be a powerful blood goddess. (The idiots bought it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T11:04:53-08:00","id":409128,"title":"","content":"In the elder campaign I played in, one player had his character get miffed at all the other PCs for reasons I can't recall and tried to buddy up with a nomadic Sabbat pack so he could steer them into hunting down the rest of the group. But he did it so ineptly - he seemed to think just showing up out of the blue at a mass embrace/shovelhead party and claiming solidarity would somehow ensure the loyalty of a dedicated pack of cultists he'd just met. It was like watching Marie Antoinette cozy up to a bunch of revolutionaries and ask if they could spare some cake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T16:27:33-08:00","id":409399,"title":"","content":"So. We're playing an Arabian Nights game influenced by the WoD and running on Adventure! rules. The group meets up, tricks some bandits into getting themselves into trouble instead of fighting them and finds out that in the streets of Baghdad there is a group of thieves who are running a highly efficient operation. The characters find out an item they are looking for was stolen by the thieves and they work out the thieves are hiding themselves by using animals to steal for them.<br /> <br /> They track the item down to a blind beggar and his monkey. The beggar has no idea what they're talking about, but the monkey seems to know too much. The Dervish grabs him by the throat and the party discusses how to find his bosses/trainers. At this point one of the members (a Basran scholar) decides that he has a solution. He asks the wandering Indian cook if he has any spicy peppers. The cook is confused (As are the rest of us), but of course he does - the running shtick of the character is that he is travelling the world to find the greatest recipes and the greatest spices. The scholar takes the super-strong pepper and proceeds to stuff it up the monkey's butt.<br /> <br /> ... at this point the cast is looking in shock. The ST is stumped, the rest of us don't know if we are supposed to laugh or be creeped out. The ST moves it along by making the monkey run like hell and the Dervish and my Old storyteller do their best to try and keep an eye on it. We track it to the docks and the ST ends the session there.<br /> <br /> The game was never continued. The ST told me that after the pepper he just had no more idea what to do with us after that pepper. Dropping the player with the idea was not an option as he's a close friend to all of us, and he's usually the sensible sort...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T18:45:22-08:00","id":409485,"title":"","content":"Post-Apocalyptic Game. Sign outside of town has graffiti that says &quot;Population: 666&quot;. We head in, take a look around, and a horde of zombies comes out. We dispatch one as we retreat to our jeep. We speed off, pedal to the metal, and one player decides he just has to adjust the population sign for the zombie we killed. Everyone else says no, so he jumps out of the moving vehicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T04:49:30-08:00","id":409907,"title":"","content":"A game almost 10 years ago<br /> Someone dethroned the prince, and an almost all-out-war brake out. Elders forging alliances, ancillae shifting alliances, neonates willing to support almost anyone asking them, gangs of Anarchs roaming the rack, the occasional Sabbat pack sticking its neck in the beehive (and being punctually beheaded) and the caitiff population trying to figure out is they can replicate the Maldavis trick...<br /> In the end, after almost 12 nights/plays of force and politicks, our coterie conquer the city. The Ventrue become prince, the Tremere Seneschal, the Gangrel is the new Sheriff, and the Setite (don't ask) the Keeper of Elysium.<br /> Ok, fine. We're in charge, now the fun begins...<br /> or not...<br /> <br /> The Gehenna explode in all it fullness. In a couple of plays the city is burning. Then, Saulot step in (Saulot step in ALWAYS, if there is a Gehenna going on...) and start telling the council of the city (our coterie) what to do for saving the city and therefore the Cainite race.<br /> Then, the Ventrue blow up &lt;This is my city! You can't just come in and trying to give orders! Did you hear? MY CITY! Then fuck you, fuck you and go somewhere else spouting your damn crap!&gt; (going on for 10 minutes, timed).<br /> <br /> In the end, our Storyteller facepalm. He check the Frenzy for Saulot, botch...<br /> <br /> oh well, at least it was a great battle, against a frenzied antediluvian...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","user":"Ryoga84","date":". 02-19-2015, 05:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T17:58:19-07:00","id":452188,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I was playing a gangrel in a coterie with 2 other players, a malkavian and I think it was a brujah. The story revolved around the idea that the government found out about kindred and founded an agency to study and eradicate them. There came a point in which our characters would have benefited from stealing some research from a facility, but it was pretty suicidal. So, having no powers like domination or presence, and not having 3 nights to blood bond someone, I decided to try... animalism on one of the chimpanzees in the local zoo, which the malk would then obfuscate to avoid detection (we weren't clear on the rules for obfuscate range back then). It... didn't go well, the chimp was detected and killed, but to this day his sacrifice has not been forgotten. I know chimps are technically primates, but we still refer to it as &quot;the little obfuscated monkey&quot;.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5246-warlock","name":"Warlock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}